# Detection 014 – Disabled User Account Monitoring

## 1. Overview

Windows Security Event ID 4725 is generated when a user account is disabled.

Disabling accounts is a normal administrative activity, but unauthorized account disabling may indicate malicious activity.

Possible concerns include:
- Disabling security administrators.
- Disrupting employee access.
- Disabling accounts used by security teams.
- Covering tracks after unauthorized access.
- Interfering with incident response.

## 2. Objective

Detect disabled user accounts, identify who performed the action, and investigate whether the change was authorized.

## 3. Windows Event Information

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| Event ID | 4725 |
| Event Name | A user account was disabled |
| Log Source | Windows Security |
| Systems | Windows endpoints and Domain Controllers |
| Severity | Context-dependent |

